persist-public-only-objects: TPM2_EvictControl may make a public-only object persistent

Classification: spec-deviation bug fix.

Specification (TPM 2.0 Part 3, revision 185, TPM2_EvictControl): "If
*objectHandle* references a Transient Object: 1. The TPM shall return
`TPM_RC_ATTRIBUTES` if 1. it is in the hierarchy of `TPM_RH_NULL` or a
firmware-limited or SVN-limited hierarchy, or [...] 2. the *stClear* is SET in
the object or in an ancestor key." with the note "Older versions of the
specification did not allow an object to be persisted when only the public
portion of the object was loaded (for NV space efficiency). Support for
persisting public-only objects was added in version 185."

This reference still implements the older rule and rejects an object with
attributes.publicOnly SET (e.g. the public-only object of
TPM2_LoadExternal(hierarchy = TPM_RH_OWNER)) with TPM_RC_ATTRIBUTES +
RC_EvictControl_objectHandle. tpm-rs (TPM_SPEC_VERSION 185) and the TCG
reference v185.0.0 (`mstpm20-185-feature`, which already dropped the check) persist it.
The check now rejects only temporary and stClear objects, as in v185; the
persistent copy keeps attributes.publicOnly (NvAddEvictObject stores the whole
OBJECT), so it still has neither authValue nor authPolicy available.
Found by differential fuzzing.
diff --git a/src/ContextCommands.c b/src/ContextCommands.c
--- a/src/ContextCommands.c
+++ b/src/ContextCommands.c
@@ -541,10 +541,12 @@
        || HierarchyIsSvnLimited(evictObject->hierarchy))
 	return TPM_RCS_HIERARCHY + RC_EvictControl_objectHandle;
 
-    // Temporary, stClear or public only objects can not be made persistent
+    // tpm-rs differential testing -- C-ref spec deviation fix (NOT determinism):
+    // public-only objects may be made persistent since revision 185 of Part 3
+    // (TPM2_EvictControl); only temporary and stClear objects are rejected.
+    // Temporary or stClear objects can not be made persistent
     if(evictObject->attributes.temporary == SET
-       || evictObject->attributes.stClear == SET
-       || evictObject->attributes.publicOnly == SET)
+       || evictObject->attributes.stClear == SET)
 	return TPM_RCS_ATTRIBUTES + RC_EvictControl_objectHandle;
 
     // If objectHandle refers to a persistent object, it should be the same as
